  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 101 PM MDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nFor Sunday into Monday, we will warm up again, with temperatures \nbeing similar to today temps. However, pop chance will be quite a \nbit better for Sunday over the CONTDVD. and we may see a good chance \nof storms regionwide Monday afternoon and evening, especially if a \ncool front can get in here during the afternoon and bring showers \nand storms to the plains during Monday evening. \n\nBoth deterministic and statistical guidance shows a sharp drop-off \nin temps for Tuesday. The statistical guidance is more confident \ntoday then it was yesterday as there is much less of a range in \ntemps and it cools it off a good 15F over the plains with temps just \na bit cooler over the mtns/valleys.\n\nPops on Tuesday are going to be in the scattered to likely category, \nespecially along the greater mtn/plains interface as synoptically \nforced upslope flow develops over the region. The combination of the \nmonsoon plume aloft and moist sfc upslope will bring a threat of \nheavier rain to the region, and burn scar flooding will be on the \nincrease.\n\nWednesday into late week we will continue to see a good chance of \nrain over the region as another front will push through late WED and \nTHU and the monsoon tap will continue. \n\nOverall, next week looks cooler and wetter over the region. \n\\/Hodanish",
